Ath-ja-hakar.

544
00:44:09,430 --> 00:44:11,500
Athjahakar.

545
00:44:12,610 --> 00:44:15,720
Well, I suppose I'm a bit out of practice.

546
00:44:16,740 --> 00:44:19,430
Your High Valyrian is very good, Your Grace.

547
00:44:20,060 --> 00:44:22,610
The gods could not devise a more perfect tongue.

548
00:44:23,320 --> 00:44:25,850
It is the only proper language for poetry.

549
00:44:31,660 --> 00:44:33,940
No screaming or she dies.

550
00:44:48,050 --> 00:44:49,290
What do you want?

551
00:44:51,010 --> 00:44:51,790
You.

552
00:44:52,100 --> 00:44:53,360
Let her go.

553
00:44:53,900 --> 00:44:56,080
Don't scream, lovely girl.

554
00:45:03,600 --> 00:45:05,500
You were sent here to kill me?

555
00:45:06,680 --> 00:45:07,980
So why haven't you?

556
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:10,900
I don't want to.

557
00:45:11,730 --> 00:45:13,760
What do your captains have to say about that?

558
00:45:13,920 --> 00:45:15,180
You should ask them.

559
00:45:21,460 --> 00:45:22,420
Why?

560
00:45:22,880 --> 00:45:25,210
We had philosophical differences.

561
00:45:25,210 --> 00:45:27,950
- Over what? - Your beauty.

562
00:45:28,360 --> 00:45:30,490
It meant more to me than it did to them.

563
00:45:30,980 --> 00:45:32,240
You're a strange man.

564
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:34,110
I'm the simplest man you'll ever meet.

565
00:45:34,770 --> 00:45:36,170
I only do what I want to do.

566
00:45:36,400 --> 00:45:38,380
And this is supposed to impress me?

567
00:45:39,060 --> 00:45:39,840
Yes.

568
00:45:42,100 --> 00:45:44,830
Why would I trust a man who murders his comrades?

569
00:45:45,310 --> 00:45:47,270
They ordered me to murder you.

570
00:45:47,560 --> 00:45:49,630
I told them I preferred not to.

571
00:45:49,630 --> 00:45:51,500
They told me I had no choice.

572
00:45:52,210 --> 00:45:53,960
I told them I am Daario Naharis.

573
00:45:54,150 --> 00:45:56,620
I always have a choice.

574
00:45:58,400 --> 00:45:59,760
They drew their swords

575
00:46:01,160 --> 00:46:02,550
and I drew mine.

576
00:46:34,250 --> 00:46:35,820
Will you fight for me?

577
00:46:43,390 --> 00:46:44,720
Swear to me.

578
00:46:48,150 --> 00:46:51,070
The Second Sons are yours and so is Daario Naharis.

579
00:46:51,760 --> 00:46:54,070
My sword is yours, my life is yours,

580
00:46:54,590 --> 00:46:56,140
my heart is yours.

581
00:47:15,070 --> 00:47:17,230
You really ought to knock.

582
00:47:17,230 --> 00:47:18,510
I brought your breakfast.

583
00:48:37,280 --> 00:48:38,580
It's getting dark.

584
00:48:39,450 --> 00:48:40,930
We could stay here for the night.

585
00:49:14,450 --> 00:49:16,600
How hard can it be to build a fire?

586
00:49:17,390 --> 00:49:18,810
It doesn't matter.

587
00:49:19,160 --> 00:49:21,370
Come under the furs. We can keep each other warm.

588
00:49:41,510 --> 00:49:43,120
He winked at me before.

589
00:49:44,530 --> 00:49:48,160
- I doubt it. - I saw him wink at me.

590
00:49:48,400 --> 00:49:49,640
He blinked.

591
00:49:50,920 --> 00:49:53,440
I suppose it's a rather philosophical difference

592
00:49:53,440 --> 00:49:55,690
between a wink and a blink.

593
00:49:56,680 --> 00:49:57,440
A what?

594
00:50:00,420 --> 00:50:03,600
Well, I mean, there's no real difference.

595
00:50:06,610 --> 00:50:08,610
A wink is on purpose.

596
00:50:12,140 --> 00:50:13,630
You thought of a name yet?

597
00:50:18,350 --> 00:50:20,570
It would be easier to refer to him if he had a name.

598
00:50:20,570 --> 00:50:23,410
Sometimes do you talk fancy on purpose to confuse me?

599
00:50:23,630 --> 00:50:25,910
What? No.

600
00:50:26,590 --> 00:50:28,620
This is just the way I talk.

601
00:50:32,320 --> 00:50:33,910
I'll build that fire.

602
00:50:42,820 --> 00:50:44,810
Don't you think he should have a name?

603
00:50:46,870 --> 00:50:48,940
I don't know many boys' names.

604
00:50:50,110 --> 00:50:51,070
Let's see,

605
00:50:51,270 --> 00:50:53,250
there's Duncan,

606
00:50:54,330 --> 00:50:55,680
Kevan, Jon...

607
00:50:57,380 --> 00:50:58,190
Guymon,

608
00:50:58,190 --> 00:51:00,590
Feldan, Tristifer.

609
00:51:00,780 --> 00:51:01,610
Craster.

610
00:51:03,430 --> 00:51:04,950
Uh, yes.

611
00:51:06,580 --> 00:51:07,920
Maybe that's not--

612
00:51:08,120 --> 00:51:09,210
Mormont.

613
00:51:10,290 --> 00:51:11,910
That's a lovely idea,

614
00:51:12,640 --> 00:51:14,380
but Mormont's a last name.

615
00:51:15,210 --> 00:51:16,900
Why is it a last name?

616
00:51:17,750 --> 00:51:20,070
Well, it's a family name.

617
00:51:22,150 --> 00:51:24,490
For instance, I'm Samwell Tarly.

618
00:51:25,080 --> 00:51:27,040
Samwell is my birth name

619
00:51:27,360 --> 00:51:29,940
and Tarly is my family name.

620
00:51:31,260 --> 00:51:34,980
You see? So my father is also a Tarly.

621
00:51:36,700 --> 00:51:38,530
His name is Samwell Tarly, too?

622
00:51:38,530 --> 00:51:41,250
No, Randyll Tarly.

623
00:51:41,320 --> 00:51:43,150
Randyll is a handsome name.

624
00:51:44,970 --> 00:51:46,530
Please don't name him Randyll.

625
00:51:51,020 --> 00:51:53,000
Is your father cruel like mine?

626
00:51:57,490 --> 00:51:59,240
Different manner of cruel.

627
00:52:12,730 --> 00:52:13,980
Not Randyll, then.

628
00:52:37,480 --> 00:52:38,240
Don't.

629
00:52:39,810 --> 00:52:41,130
Don't go out there.

630
00:52:41,550 --> 00:52:42,490
I'll be back.

631
00:52:43,350 --> 00:52:44,500
I just want to look.

632
00:53:20,900 --> 00:53:21,990
Go inside.

633
00:53:23,890 --> 00:53:25,680
Go back inside. I'll--

634
00:53:39,110 --> 00:53:40,840
It's come for the baby.

635
00:53:57,020 --> 00:53:58,190
Stay back!

636
00:54:06,010 --> 00:54:07,560
You stay back!

637
00:54:19,770 --> 00:54:22,200
No, you can't have him! No!

638
00:54:24,920 --> 00:54:25,720
No!

